    "title": "Diocese of Sioux City Superintendent to resign - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Reilly Mahon Maren Ewertz ,\n1 hours ago SIOUX CITY , Iowa ( KCAU ) — A Siouxland Catholic school district superintendent is resigning.\nThe Diocese of Sioux City announced that Patty Lansink will leave her role effective February 27.\nOfficials said she accepted a regional vice president position with Facts Education Services.\nStory continues below\nLansink has been with the Diocese since being hired in 2014 as a part-time assistant superintendent.\nShe took on the top role only four years after being hired.\nDiocese officials said that the search for a new superintendent will begin in the coming years.\nCopyright 2026 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to KCAU 9 News | Sioux City, IA | News, Weather, and Sports.",
    "summary": "By Reilly Mahon Maren Ewertz , 1 hours ago SIOUX CITY , Iowa ( KCAU ) — A Siouxland Catholic school district superintendent is resigning. The Diocese of Sioux City announced that Patty Lansink will leave her role effective February 27. Officials said she accepted a regional vice president position with Facts Education Services. Lansink has been with the Diocese since being hired in 2014 as a part-time assistant superintendent. Diocese officials said that the search for a new superintendent will begin in the coming years.",
